{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Full-tier run: 4 failures triaged — 1 was MINE, 3 pre-existing\n\n**Final commit `39ca21aea606846c483975f7d0715dd359dea052`** (supersedes `e2ca5803298b` and\n`ce3b62144aeb`). 26 files, +809/-88. Trailer verified.\n\nRunning the FULL `tests/unit` tier — the coverage gap that let the module-size breach through —\nsurfaced **13996 passed, 4 failed, 51 skipped**. I did not assume those were pre-existing; I\ntested it.\n\n### The discriminating experiment\n\nMy work was committed, so I detached the same worktree onto `origin/main` — same venv, same\neditable install, same host — ran the four, then returned to my branch. That isolates *my change*\nas the only variable.\n\n| test | on `origin/main` | verdict |\n|---|---|---|\n| `test_doctor_dirty_tree::…heals_the_seeded_wedge_end_to_end` | FAILS | pre-existing |\n| `test_doctor_dirty_tree::…idempotent_on_a_clean_store` | FAILS | pre-existing |\n| `test_doctor_mapping::…mapping_warning_only_yields_zero_exit` | FAILS | pre-existing |\n| `test_check_criteria_vocabulary::…rejects_live_vocabulary_through_guard` | PASSES | **MINE** |\n\n### The 3 pre-existing failures are HOST-ENVIRONMENT, not repo defects\n\n`doctor_cli([\"--repair\"])` returns 1 on a *clean* store because `doctor` inspects the\n**operator's own** MCP client configuration and finds real problems on this machine:\n\n    codex   [error] pat-unresolvable:     REBAR_CODEX_PAT unset in this environment\n    copilot [error] pat-literal-in-config: ~/.copilot/mcp-config.json\n    claude  [error] pat-literal-in-config: ~/.claude.json\n\nSo they fail for anyone whose host MCP configs are in that state, independent of the tree. Not a\nflake, not a regression — a host-coupled test. Out of scope here; worth its own ticket if it is\nbiting other sessions on this box.\n\n### The 4th failure was mine, and the fix is the fixture's own documented convention\n\n    python: can't open file '<tmp>/scripts/check_tickets_boundary.py': No such file or directory\n    make: *** [lint] Error 2\n\n`test_make_lint_rejects_live_vocabulary_through_guard` builds a synthetic minimal tree and runs\nthe **real committed Makefile** in it. My new `make lint` step invoked a script that tree does not\ncontain, so `make lint` aborted before reaching the vocabulary guard under test — the test failed\non a missing file rather than on its subject.\n\nThe fixture anticipates exactly this and says so in a comment:\n\n> *\"A new `make lint` gate needs a stub here or it aborts the run early and this test fails on a\n> missing script rather than on the guard.\"*\n\nThree prior stories (raw-git-writes, wall-clock-asserts, destructive-test-exec) each added a stub\nplus a one-line comment. I did the same, in the same style. **This is fixture maintenance the test\nitself mandates, not test-weakening**: no assertion was removed, loosened, or skipped — the guard\nstill runs and still has to reject `src/rebar/live.py:1`. `48 passed`.\n\n### Verification at the final commit\n\n    module-size gate (CI's exact awk command) .... OK — none over 800\n    check_tickets_boundary.py .................... exit 0\n    oracle + guards + vocab + module-size ........ 73 passed\n    make lint .................................... exit 0\n    make typecheck ............................... Success: 678 source files\n    verify-commit-ticket --rev 39ca21aea606 ...... OK - resolved 0514-92e0-e6c4-4304\n\nA confirmatory full `tests/unit` + `tests/interfaces` run is in flight; I expect exactly the 3\nhost-coupled doctor failures and nothing else.\n\n### Lesson worth keeping\n\nAdding a step to `make lint` has **two** obligations beyond the step itself: the CI-only gates it\ndoes not cover (module-size — how the 804-LOC breach escaped), and every test that executes the\nreal Makefile in a synthetic tree. I hit both, in that order, and neither was visible from a green\n`make lint`."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787865690399662705,"uuid":"6a652125-4db6-4191-b5b4-497db6a47826"}